title: CompoundFieldsImport
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A `text/vnd.tiddlywiki-multiple+fields` tiddler exports with its compound `text` and every derived field, so a wiki without this feature still sees ordinary fields. Editing a field there and importing the tiddler back leaves that field and the text in disagreement. The rule on import:

* Into a wiki that does not hold the tiddler, or holds it with a different compound text: the text wins and the differing fields take its values
* Over a local copy whose compound text is unchanged: the field values win and are written into the text, exactly as a field write inside this wiki is

The import dialog lists the differing fields beside the tiddler and names the side that is kept, so the import can be cancelled and reconciled by hand.
